body:
This test is titled “renders drag handles when enableReorder is true” but it never asserts that a handle actually renders (e.g., via `.cursor-grab` or `getByLabelText('Drag to reorder')`). As written, it would still pass if the handle wiring regressed. Add an explicit assertion for the drag handle so the test matches its intent.
```suggestion
      // DndContext renders sortable wrappers and exposes drag handles
      expect(screen.getByText('Item A')).toBeTruthy();
      expect(screen.getByText('Item B')).toBeTruthy();
      const grips = container.querySelectorAll('.cursor-grab');
      expect(grips.length).toBeGreaterThan(0);
```
